// What the entry point may be declared to take.
//
// Nothing. The entry point is the C `main`, which the platform calls with
// (argc, argv), so a declared parameter was built out of whatever the
// registers happened to hold: `main(string[] args)` compiled, `args.length`
// read 913878280, and `args[1]` passed the bounds check and read past the end.
// About half the runs segfaulted and the other half printed the right answer,
// which is the worst shape a defect can take -- it was found while
// benchmarking, not by a test.
//
// Command-line arguments have their own way in (`std.env.args()`,
// `std.env.argAt`, `std.env.argsCount`), which reads them from the operating
// system and works on every target, so the declaration is refused rather than
// given a second and quieter path.
//
// Compiled for the diagnostic, so the file never runs.

int32 main(string[] args) {
    return args.length;
}
